course: dictionary
lesson: 3459
title: Failure and learning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Failure means not succeeding at something you tried to do. It can also mean a plan or attempt that did not work, or a machine that stops working. Read the words around it to find the right meaning: «The power failure left the whole street in the dark» tells you the electricity stopped working.
explain: Look at «Failures are how you learn.» Here failure does not mean you are bad at something. It means a try that did not work, and that try still teaches you something. Swap in your meaning: "Tries that did not work are how you learn" still makes sense.
explain: Failure stings because you cared. «Failure stings because you cared; the trick is to hear "not yet" instead of "never".» So when you fail, look at what you learned, and measure yourself against your own last try, not against someone else.
fact: Failure means not succeeding at something you tried to do.
fact: A failure can be an attempt, plan or thing that did not work.
fact: A failure of a machine is when it stops working, like «a power failure».
fact: «Failure to follow the rules» means not doing what the rules ask you to do.
fact: Scientists and inventors often fail many times before they succeed, so failure is part of learning.
exercise: «The power failure left the whole street in the dark.» What does failure mean here? | A visit from a friend | A party with lots of games | A test that was very easy | *A power supply that stopped working
exercise: Which words suggest that failure is part of learning? | Failure is always the end | Failure means you are bad at everything | Never try again | *Failures are how you learn
exercise: «The plan ended in failure.» What does ended in failure mean? | It was finished early by a bell | It was given a prize | *It did not work | It was a big success
test: In the text, what is «a setback»? | A small step forward | A bet on a game | A new friend | *A failure made to sound like a small step back
test: What is the best way to hear a failure, according to the text? | *Hear "not yet" and look at what you learned | Hide the test paper | Blame your friends | Hear "never" and give up
exam: According to the text, what should you measure yourself against after a failure? | *Your own last try | Nobody at all | A perfect score in every test | Your friend who passed
